2.2 E(2) - steerable feature fields
Steerable CNNs define feature spaces as spaces of steerable feature fields f : R2 → Rc which
associate a c-dimensional feature vector f (x) ∈ Rc to each point x of a base space, in our case the plane R2. In contrast to vanilla CNNs, the feature fields of steerable CNNs are associated with a transformation law which specifies their transformation under actions of E(2) (or subgroups) and therefore endows features with a notion of orientation1. Formally, a feature vector f (x) encodes the coefficients of a coordinate independent geometric feature relative to a choice of reference frame or, equivalently, image orientation (see Appendix A).
