As a final experiment on MNIST rot we are replicating the regular C16 model from [7] which was the previous SOTA. It is mostly similar to the models evaluated in the previous sections but is wider, uses larger kernel sizes and adds additional fully connected layers; see Table 14 in the Appendix. As reported in Table 5, our reimplementation matches the accuracy of the original model. Replacing the regular feature fields with the quotient representations used in Section 3.1 leads to slightly better results. We refer to Appendix C for more insights on the improved performance of the quotient model. A further significant improvement and a new state of the art is being achieved by a D16-equivariant model, which is restricted to C16 after the penultimate layer.
